# K6 by stage, gb10e (GB10 X925 cpu 7 under the timing lock; builds on the A725s), 2026-10-06 18:02-18:27Z, load
# 0.0-1.4 (the first runs, run.out, started 18:02Z, before the window post at 18:05Z; every run under the lock).
# The kernel is master c008952's src/asm/arm64/k6_neon.S. Timing-only variants each stop after one stage or drop
# one piece of work; K6 runs alone over one class of pieces (bench_cut: tests/bpe/bench_neon.c with the timed
# cell restricted to the pieces over 15 bytes ("long") or the 2..15-byte pieces the words table does not answer
# ("short"), and no exactness check: a variant that stops early answers wrong by design). Best of 5 rounds a run, 3-4
# cycles in rotating order, the c twin timed beside each run as a drift control. Pieces: tests/bpe/gen.py streams of
# the bench corpus with hf 0.23.2's ids (llama3 / o200k en, llama3 code, llama3 / qwen38 zh, llama3 / qwen38 ml).
#   base   k6_neon.S as it is
#   pm     stop after the premerge walk (n_out 0)                 spm    pm, and the byte path stops after its init
#   pmn    pm without the char table's two loads (every char taken, never risky)
#   recs   stop after the records (output the symbols)           srecs  recs, and the byte path stops after its init
#   r1     stop after round one and the first scan (no merge loop) sr1  r1, and the byte path stops after its init
#   r1b    r1 with round one's bucket probe dropped (the filter's branch kept)            sr1b  likewise
#   r1x    r1 with round one's filter bits computed and unused (no branch, no probe)      sr1x  likewise
#   rb     round one in two passes (an experiment, exact: the filter bits without a branch, a survivor list, then the
#          probes; test_bpe_neon 5,942,777 checks 0 failures; bench_neon exact on llama3 / qwen38 zh and ml, the
#          last section: bench_neon.c with its K6 check on check.c's rule, built against rb's library)
# The variants are diffs against k6_neon.S at c008952; bench_cut.c is a diff against bench_neon.c at c008952 (the
# first long-only runs, run.out, used its earlier form, which built the same long list). Then every run's output.

